section.subsection:
The tax credit allowed by Subsection (2) claimed on a return filed under this part shall be reduced by $.025 for each dollar by which modified adjusted gross income for purposes of the return exceeds:

for a federal individual income tax return that is allowed a married filing separately status, $16,000;
for a federal individual income tax return that is allowed a single filing status, $25,000;
for a federal individual income tax return that is allowed a head of household filing status, $32,000; or
for a return under this chapter that is allowed a joint filing status, $32,000.
